    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4717": {
      "title": "Faculty of Arts, Journalism and Communications",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Faculty of Arts, Journalism and Communications Department/Faculty Office of the President Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 12 MONTHS Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4717 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): We are seeking a Student Assistant to support the Faculty of Arts, Journalism and Communications . The student will provide assistance in researching, interviewing, writing, and editing for the KPU 50th anniversary book project. PRINCIPAL DUTIES Fact-finding about KPU’s history and various individuals involved in KPU Interviewing people involved in KPU Transcribing interviews and writing profiles of people involved in KPU Editing other students’ written work Reviewing profiles with interviewees Creating and maintaining the project website and social media accounts REQUIREMENTS Strong written and verbal communication skills Must be a journalism or creative writing student Reliable and hardworking Familiarity with basic principles of web design and social media Interested in history and post-secondary education This position is reserved for KPU Students only. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4829": {
      "title": "Future Students' Office Student Ambassador",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Future Students' Office Student Ambassador Department/Faculty Student Services - Registrar's Office Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 6 Months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4829 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Regular travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): SUMMARY The Student Assistant will work with team members in the Future Students' Office on a variety of recruitment initiatives. He/she performs student engagement and recruitment related activities, as well as assists with events and other activities and general duties as needed. Successful Student Assistants are enthusiastic, outgoing, quick-thinking, and possess creative problem-solving skills. They are passionate about sharing their experiences at KPU with prospective students and parents. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. PRINCIPLE DUTIES Engage with prospective students through various channels (events etc.) Assist events team with planning, setup, coordination and operation logistics. Assist with communications activities to prospective students. Assist recruiters with presentations in communities from a student perspective. Assist in promoting events to current and prospective KPU students. Assist in preparing information packages/giveaway bags for campus tours Act as an ambassador for the University at external events creating a positive rapport with prospective students and community. COMMUNICATIONS DUTIES Assist with preparing mailing packages to prospects, students, and other audiences. OTHER DUTIES Assist with photocopying, and collation of materials for mail-outs and promotions. Assist with data collection, compilation, and interpretation. REQUIREMENTS Working towards a diploma or degree at KPU. Creative, energetic, outgoing and enthusiastic-seeking to make a difference. A strong social media user with a desire to contribute content and learn about processes, procedures and best practices. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to communicate clearly with others. Excellent customer service skills. Reliable, organized and detail oriented. Ability to effectively multi-task. Public speaking experience is an asset. Sensitive to diverse student needs. A second language is an asset, but not required. Problem solver, works independently and meets deadlines. Working Knowledge of Microsoft Office. Available to work evenings and weekends as needed. AVAILABILITY Work schedule will be approximately 8 - 12 hours weekly. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4852": {
      "title": "GAME DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTOR",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description GAME DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTOR Department/Faculty Faculty of Arts Home Campus (Location) Faculty - All Campuses Employment Duration QFL Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4852 Internal Closing Date: October 24, 2026 External Closing Date: October 24, 2026 # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Qualified Faculty List Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ENTERTAINMENT ARTS - GAME DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE: QFL (Qualified Faculty List) POSITION START: January 1, 2027 KPU proudly offers all learners opportunities to achieve success in a diverse range of programs that blend theory and practice, critical understanding, and social and ethical awareness necessary for good citizenship and rewarding careers. FACULTY OVERVIEW: Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is the fourth largest university in the province of British Columbia and serves communities in the South Fraser region and beyond.  A leader in innovative, interdisciplinary education with a teaching-focused mandate, KPU offers all learners opportunities to achieve the highest standards of academic performance. Our many programs of study provide applied learning and broad-based university education. Within KPU, the Faculty of Arts has over 6000 full-time students and over 300 faculty members from across the Humanities and Social Sciences. The Faculty of Arts includes 19 departments and 21 programs at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The Faculty is also home to two Canada Research Chairs: the first in Lifespan Cognition, and the second in South Asian Literary and Cultural Studies. Many of our programs offer opportunities for experiential education through practicums, co-ops, international field-schools and exchanges, service learning, community engagement, and research collaborations. For more information about the Faculty of Arts, please visit our website at: https://www.kpu.ca/arts . POSITION OVERVIEW: The Entertainment Arts program within the Faculty of Arts at Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) seeks to establish a list of faculty qualified to teach in the program and who will be eligible for future course contracts on a per-semester basis. Applications are invited from individuals with expertise related to the fields of Game Design and Development , and the areas listed below. Courses may be offered during the day or evening, online or in-person at KPU’s Richmond campus, and faculty are expected to be available to teach in either delivery mode. Video Game Design experience in a senior or better role on at least two shipped titles, especially in the fields of: Level Design System Design Direct experience with technical and in-engine design tools, especially Unreal and Unity Must provide evidence of relevant design knowledge and experience Strong understanding of the intersection of various game development fields, including narrative, programming, technical design, game art, production (but not necessarily direct experience in all of these) Strong presentation and English communication skills Ability to provide verbal and written feedback to students to improve their work Comfort and experience with conflict resolution techniques For more information about Entertainment Arts course offerings, please consult the following link: https://calendar.kpu.ca/courses-az/enta/ More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: Preference will be given to individuals who have previously taught courses in a field of study listed above, who have significant professional, industry-related experience acquired within the last three years, and who have a record of teaching excellence at the post-secondary level. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates are asked to submit: A link to Demo reel on CV and Cover Letter A cover letter which clearly identifies: The field(s) of study in which you are qualified to teach The type of position in which you are interested: a one-year position at 50% or more (Non-regular, Type 2), and/or single-semester contract work of three or fewer sections (Non-regular, Type 1) A curriculum vitae with links to a portfolio site Evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., course evaluations, student survey results, peer review reports, past syllabi, or equivalent) A statement of teaching philosophy that discusses important elements of your teaching, such as: How it is informed by your professional, industry-related experience How it incorporates approaches to equity, diversity, inclusion, and decolonization The names and contact information of three referees able to comment on your teaching ability and professional, industry-related experience. Please note that incomplete applications will not be considered. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. This competition is for successful candidates to be added to our Qualified Faculty List. When work in this area becomes available, the Qualified Faculty List will be drawn upon to assign work. As such, please indicate on your application your preferred workload percentage. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4821": {
      "title": "Health Science Instructor, Qualified Faculty List",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Health Science Instructor, Qualified Faculty List Department/Faculty Faculty of Science Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration Qualified Faculty List Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4821 Internal Closing Date: September 25, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 5 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Qualified Faculty List Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): HEALTH SCIENCE INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE: QUALIFIED FACULTY LIST FACULTY OVERVIEW: As Canada’s only polytechnic university, Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is the fourth largest university in the province of British Columbia and serves communities in the South Fraser region and beyond. A Leader in innovative education with a teaching-focused mandate, KPU offers all learners opportunities to achieve the highest standards of academic performance. Within KPU, the Faculty of Science has over 1,500 full-time students and over 200 faculty members and instructors from across the natural and applied sciences. Faculty of Science includes nine departments and over 30 programs at the undergraduate level, with offerings at all four KPU campuses. The faculty is also home to Canada Research Chair: Dr. Cayley Velazquez and Sherman Jen Research Chair, Dr. Paul Adams. The Faculty of Science offers experiential learning through hands-on curriculum and co-ops and research collaboration opportunities with KPU’s Institute for Sustainable Horticulture (ISH), Institute of Sustainable Food Systems (ISFS), and Applied Genomics Center (AGC). As well, our faculty is home to over a hectare of horticulture field lab and working farm and a state-of-the art brewery, which has been recognized internationally and locally, winning BC Brewery of the Year in 2019. For more information about the Faculty of Science, please visit our website at: kpu.ca/science POSITION OVERVIEW: Kwantlen Polytechnic University’s Faculty of Science is currently seeking applications for Health Science instructors to join the Department of Biological and Health Sciences Qualified Faculty List for the Health Science Degree Program. We welcome applications from qualified instructors with research expertise or industry/sector experience in health policy, administration and leadership, allied health, business, and/or clinical research and development. Experience in the areas of health informatics, analytics, data science, and precision medicine are an asset. Courses may include Introduction to Health Science and upper-level topics such as Health Business, Health Program Planning and Evaluation, Populations and Policy, Applications to Health Science, Pharmacology, Nutrition, Health and Aging, and Critical Evaluation. Health Science is a recently developed and rapidly growing undergraduate program offered within the Department of Biological and Health Sciences at KPU. We provide an experiential learning approach in which students gain foundational knowledge in the basic sciences and practical knowledge in clinical, public, community and population health to understand current and emerging health issues and the policies, systems, and technology used to advance health and wellness. We offer a Bachelor of Science in Health Science degree, along with honours, minor, and co-op options. Successful applicants will work collaboratively with department members and colleagues across the broader KPU community to continue shaping this exciting program. More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: We seek a scholar who possesses, at minimum, a Master’s degree (Ph.D. preferred) in health science, public health, public administration, human biology, or another equivalent field. The ideal candidate will have excellent written and oral communication skills as well as recent post-secondary teaching or equivalent research, scholarly, or professional experience demonstrating currency in a health science related discipline. We are looking for a scholar that is excited to develop connections to industry and/or community partners to advance course-based experiential learning opportunities. Those interested in applying can find more information on our courses by visiting our website at: https://www.kpu.ca/science/health-science APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates are asked to submit: Statement of teaching philosophy (maximum one page) Description of how you will incorporate your research, professional experience and/or network to support undergraduate teaching (maximum one page) Current curriculum vitae that includes information about previous courses taught and/or relevant research, scholarly, or professional experience\\ Names of three referees willing to comment on your ability to contribute to a degree-granting Biological and Health Sciences department. Please forward your application package with cover letter. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. This competition is for successful candidates to be added to our Qualified Faculty List. When work in this area becomes available, the Qualified Faculty List will be drawn upon to assign work. As such, please indicate on your application if you are interested in being added to this list and your preferred workload percentage. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4706": {
      "title": "Indigenous Designer-in-Residence",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Indigenous Designer-in-Residence Department/Faculty Wilson School of Design Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration Please see details below Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4706 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Director, Strategy and Business Development, Wilson School of Design. SUMMARY The Wilson School of Design (WSD) invites applications from established or emerging Indigenous designers, including First Nations, Métis, and Inuit of Canada, for a position as Indigenous Designer-in-Residence. This residency will support Indigenous designers in the research and creation of new works, and is open to designers in a variety of fields, including but not restricted to fashion and apparel design, graphic design, interior design, product design, and other interdisciplinary design practices. The Indigenous Designer-in-Residence will be able to divide their time between their own creative practice and contributing to the Wilson School of Design. In their application, candidates are encouraged to detail how they envision engaging with the Wilson School of Design and the broader KPU community of faculty, students, and staff. For more information about the Wilson School of Design, please visit our website at https://www.kpu.ca/design. An applicant does not need to have to an expertise in all disciplines, but have at least one expertise and a common fundamental understanding of others. Designers will be compensated for the duration of their residency. There will also be funding available for KPU/WSD-specific events, expenses for materials and supplies, as well as for honoraria for designers whom the Indigenous Designer-in-Residence may want to invite to events. Applications should include: A curriculum vitae or resume A cover letter or video that includes your statement of interest; a proposal of the design project you will undertake during the residency; and a description of the kinds of events you would like to plan, and how you see these contributing to the KPU/WSD community. (For video submissions, please provide a link to a website or Google doc.) Please include a statement clearly indicating your availability to be present on KPU campuses (primarily the Richmond campus). A letter of support or documentation regarding your connections to Indigenous community and/or an Indigenous organization, as well as lived experience. A portfolio: up to 10 original works with titles and dates. Please provide the portfolio through a link to a website; or links to videos or audio files; or a link to a Google doc. The names of two references: One from community and one professional. KPU is committed to the Truth and Reconciliation Commission (TRC) Calls to Action and to supporting Indigenous designers and their representation and visibility within KPU and its broader communities. This program will foster community engagement and will have a positive impact on both the designers and the KPU community through sharing, dialogue, creativity, and intercultural communication. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES The organization and hosting of a series of events for the WSD and KPU that may include the following: designer talks/critiques; workshops; studio visits; outreach activities Giving guest lectures, or workshops within the WSD and KPU. Consulting with students and designers of various abilities. Participating in events organized by the WSD and/or KPU Meeting regularly with the Director, Strategy and Business Development, WSD QUALIFICATIONS Relevant community-based and/or professional experience rooted in Indigenous communities, knowledges, and traditions Designers should be active in their design discipline(s) with an established or emerging record of work as made evident through websites, exhibitions, showcases, reviews, articles, etc. A record of participation in the design community and related events Enthusiasm for connecting with KPU’s community members from a variety of areas and disciplines Willingness to organize and plan events in collaboration with the WSD Communications and Events Coordinator. SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly rate: $45.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4782": {
      "title": "Indigenous Services Student Assistant",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Indigenous Services Student Assistant Department/Faculty Student Services - Indigenous Services for Students Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 4 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4782 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): SUMMARY: Reporting to the Coordinator, Indigenous Student Transition and Engagement, the Student Assistant acts as a peer liaison and host to Indigenous students through one-on-one or small group interactions focusing on creating a safe and welcoming environment and promoting student engagement. The student assistant (also referred to as a Gathering Place Host) also supports a variety of cultural, social, and educational events at KPU. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. PRINCIPAL DUTIES: Act as a peer liaison to assist students by identifying various KPU student support services and/or make referrals to appropriate departments and/or community organizations Greet and welcome students and guests to the Gathering Place (GP) in a warm and friendly manner Promote student life activities and events Contribute to peer-run bi-monthly email newsletter and social media that highlight scholarship and funding opportunities, campus and community events Support team event planning for Indigenous cultural and community events Assist Coordinator at educational and community events, as needed Monitor GP resources and maintain bulletin board so that it is relevant and organized Assist students in the GP with computers and supplies, as needed Attend weekly departmental team meetings REQUIREMENTS: Applicant must be of Indigenous (First Nations, Métis, or Inuit) ancestry Must be enrolled at KPU as a full time student and in good academic standing Must be familiar with available student support services and campus resources Must have excellent interpersonal skills Must have experience in MS office; and knowledge of online platforms such as Moodle would be considered an asset Ability to multi-task Must be willing to travel to other campus, as needed SALARY INFORMATION: Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4809": {
      "title": "Institute for Sustainable Horticulture Research Assistant Pool",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Institute for Sustainable Horticulture Research Assistant Pool Department/Faculty Institute for Sustainable Horticulture Home Campus (Location) Langley, BC Employment Duration On-Call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4809 Internal Closing Date: December 18, 2026 External Closing Date: December 18, 2026 # of Openings: 5 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE Research Assistants report to The Director, and various project leaders involved in research with the Institute for Sustainable Horticulture. SUMMARY The Institute for Sustainable Horticulture partners with agricultural and agri-technology companies in our region to support innovation with research and development projects that promote sustainability in the sector. Current projects include developing microbial biocontrol products for pests and diseases, natural soil amendments and inoculants, biofertilizers, agritech applications, alternate growing systems, and soil microbial health. Work hours and start dates are dependent on external research grants and can be either part-time or full-time. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Greenhouse and growth chamber plant trials with biostimulants, biocontrols Laboratory trials with beneficial microbes involving sterile technique, monitoring growth and interactions Maintaining greenhouse crops, transplanting, pruning, harvesting, IPM scouting, releasing bios, cleaning pots, and general greenhouse support Soil sample collecting and processing Support field trials off site Collect, record and analyze data, assist with data interpretation and contemplate what, why and how Other duties as assigned QUALIFICATIONS These positions are suitable for students and new graduates with interest in biocontrol and horticulture, e.g. Horticulture Diploma, Plant Health Degree. The work requires a strong attention to detail and the ability to stay focused when performing repeated tasks. Some positions require travel between KPU and field sites. SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $21.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4502": {
      "title": "Lab Instructor, Faculty of Arts",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Lab Instructor, Faculty of Arts Department/Faculty Faculty of Arts Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration On-Call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4502 Internal Closing Date: March 7, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: 13 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $33.88 to $37.81 per hour Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday Hours of Work (BCGEU): On-Call Hours per Week (BCGEU): On-Call We are currently seeking a Lab Instructor to join the Faculty of Arts Job Overview This position reports to the Divisional Business Manager and works in collaboration with the Department Chair/Coordinator, instructors, and a team of Lab Instructors. The Lab Instructor assists the Faculty of Arts with overall course delivery in designated departments by assuming responsibility for reviewing material with students, student guidance and assessment (including participation in the class and lab component of any course). In addition to instructing students on lab procedures and the use of lab equipment, the Lab Instructor researches, conduct experiments, and introduces new materials, equipment and procedures to advance the program. The Lab Instructor may support any program or course offered by the relevant department(s). The class and lab assignments and learning objectives will be provided by the instructor.  Standard and prescribed industry practices will be created in collaboration between instructors, Lab Instructors, and students.  Using these, Lab Instructors are expected to perform their duties with a minimum of managerial supervision and work effectively with other Lab Instructors, faculty members, student mentors, the KPU community, and the Entertainment Arts industry. Education and Experience Graduation from a 2-year Entertainment Arts program within the past five years is required. Experience tutoring and working with students is an asset Proven junior industry-level proficiency regarding current technology and software used in the Entertainment Arts program(s) Priority will be given to candidates with experience in the specialty area of rigging. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Experience working collaboratively as an effective team player. Proven ability to take initiative when working both independently and as part of a team. Proven ability to juggle and prioritize tasks, work to meet deadlines and demands, make responsible decisions, and determine when to seek advice. Experience developing, planning, and administering systems and/or projects. Demonstrated attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment in making critical decisions. Experience in identifying problems, evaluating alternatives, consulting with stakeholders, and implementing effective solutions. Proven ability to think innovatively and creatively to implement new systems and procedures.  Evaluate their effectiveness. Experience in Microsoft Office suite (e.g. Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint, Word). Proven ability to quickly learn new software and equipment as needed. Proven ability to exercise tact, diplomacy, and resolve conflicts. Experience to providing guidance, training, and instruction to others. Demonstrated innovation and change-management skills which include supporting and encouraging new ideas and approaches to build organizational efficiency. Excellent communication, organizational, time management, and interpersonal skills is required. Demonstrated ability to maintain discretion and confidentiality is required. Please click here for a more detailed job description As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4755": {
      "title": "Laboratory Instructor, Biology",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Laboratory Instructor, Biology Department/Faculty Faculty of Science Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration On-Call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4755 Internal Closing Date: August 24, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 5 *Salary Information: 13 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $33.88 to $37.81 per hour Employment Type: On-Call Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Flex Hours Required Hours of Work (BCGEU): On-Call (varies) Hours per Week (BCGEU): On-Call (varies) We are currently seeking a Laboratory Instructor, Biology to join our Faculty of Science team. Job Overview The Laboratory Instructor - Biology participates in the Biology Department with the overall course delivery by assuming responsibility for instruction, student guidance and assessment within a lab environment. The Laboratory Instructor - Biology may be assigned to work alongside other Laboratory Instructors (or a faculty member) or alone in fulfilling the above functions. They are expected to perform with a minimum of managerial supervision by the Lab Supervisor and Dean’s Office. Lab responsibilities may involve any university level (first to fourth year) or applied program service courses offered in the Biology Department’s educational plan. Special Considerations: The Biology faculty is ultimately responsible for course delivery and development, including the laboratory portion of any course. The Laboratory Instructor - Biology assists the faculty through their role in the labs in achieving this aim.  The Lab Instructor – Biology and faculty work collegially to meet a common aim. Workload and scheduled contact hours can be found in the “WORKLOAD GUIDELINES FOR FACULTY OF SCIENCE LAB INSTRUCTORS”. The Laboratory Instructor - Biology works in compliance with current WHMIS regulations and directs students in all aspects of lab safety. They must have read the Laboratory Safety and Biosafety Manuals, completed Biosafety and Fire Safety Training and be aware of their potential role and responsibilities in the event of a chemical or biohazardous spill or accident. They must comply with all Biosafety and Biosecurity requirements of the Canadian biosafety standard of the Public Health Agency of Canada while working with Containment Level 2 organisms as it pertains to the department’s pathogens and toxins license. Education and Experience Baccalaureate degree, Masters preferred, in Biology. Proven related teaching experience is an asset. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated good working knowledge of the course content and competence in laboratory techniques pertaining to the instruction of any year biology courses. Demonstrated good working knowledge of the course content and competence in laboratory techniques pertaining to one or more of the following – introduction to biology, cell biology, microbiology, genetics, ecology, botany, marine biology, zoology, anatomy and physiology and human anatomy and physiology. Demonstrated working knowledge of the operation and routine maintenance of laboratory equipment and apparatus. Proven ability to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing. Demonstrated ability to provide instruction to undergraduate students in a laboratory setting. Demonstrated working knowledge of current WHMIS, biosafety and other preventative measures required for the safe   operation of the biology lab. Proven ability to establish and maintain effective relationships with people of varied background and experience. Proven ability to work in a team-oriented environment. Ability to travel between campuses. Please Note: When applying to this staffing process, you are not applying for a specific job, but to an inventory (or pool) for future on-call vacancies. As vacancies become available, applicants who meet the qualifications will be contacted and may require further assessment depending on the requirements of the assignment. Individuals should have a flexible schedule with the ability to work at any of our five campuses. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
