    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4823": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Research Assistant Department/Faculty Wilson School of Design Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration 6 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4823 Internal Closing Date: October 9, 2026 External Closing Date: October 9, 2026 # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): SUMMARY The Research Assistant will report to the Research Lead, typically a faculty member at Kwantlen Polytechnic University, and will help support, plan, and execute a research project or initiative. The Research Assistant may be part of an interdisciplinary research team. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES The Research Assistant may be responsible for any or all of the following: Planning and Coordination: Attend and participate in regular meetings to assist with the organization and logistics of the research project. Work in partnership with the research lead to coordinate and execute the required tasks and deliverables, including both research and administrative duties. Communication: Engage in timely and respectful verbal and written communication with the research team and external partners, as applicable. Liaise and collaborate with students, employees, and community partners. Gathering Data: Collect, organize, and analyze research data from diverse sources. Summarize and compile data with precision, paying attention to detail and context, and the requirements of the Research Ethics Board (REB), where applicable. Developing Materials: Prepare detailed summaries and high-quality reports capturing key insights. Contribute to the preparation of materials, workshops and presentations. Presenting: Develop and provide presentations about the research topic. Supporting Events (as required): Attend and provide logistical and organizational support during related research events, ensuring a welcoming and productive environment for all. QUALIFICATIONS Current or prior experience in academic or applied research, either through coursework or involvement in research projects, is desirable. Effective written and verbal communication skills to assist in writing research reports and communicating with team members. Excellent time management skills to meet project deadlines and prioritize tasks effectively. Proven ability to adapt to changes in the work environment, manage competing demands and dealing with change, delays or unexpected events, keeping constant sight of the overall objectives. Ability to think organically in an unstructured research environment, developing, and following new leads as the project grows Strong interpersonal skills including teamwork, critical thinking, and problem solving. Demonstrated ability to work independently, take initiative and overcome obstacles. Proven ability to recognize and maintain highest levels of confidentiality. Ability to maintain poise and professionalism in all types of situations. Ability to use basic office technologies (e.g., Microsoft Office suite) effectively and to adapt to new technologies that may be introduced. The ability to travel within the Lower Mainland area may be required. SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $18.25 - $22.10 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4790": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, Office of Equity and Inclusive Communities",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Research Assistant, Office of Equity and Inclusive Communities Department/Faculty Office of the Vice President, Equity & Inclusive Communities Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration March, 2027 Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4790 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 5 *Salary Information: Casual Employee - Hourly Rate Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Casual Employee Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This position reports to Dr. Asma Sayed, Canada Research Chair in South Asian Literary and Cultural Studies. SUMMARY This is a part-time position for a Research Assistant to work with and report to Canada Research Chair, Dr. Asma Sayed, on a number of research and writing projects based on South Asian literature and cinema. This position requires occasionally working in-person with the supervisor from KPU's Surrey campus. A major or minor in English, Creative Writing, Asian Studies, Film Studies, Social Justice will be given preference. Knowledge of South Asian languages such as Hindi, Gujarati, Punjabi, Urdu, etc. is an asset. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Assisting with organizing conferences, workshops, and symposiums Collaborating with the Research Associate and supporting them Researching/Locating, collating, and annotating key literature Research, editing and typing of academic journal articles and books Develop and maintain files on issues related to the current project Conduct library and online research as required Assist with photocopying, typing, filing, and overall organization of materials Communication with faculty, peers, relevant internal and external partners as directed Prepare summary reports Supporting with writing, citations, and document layout Co-authoring short pieces (author profiles, book reviews) with the supervisor Creating infographics of key findings Support with revising, editing, and analyzing written pieces Amplifying research findings and other relevant details through social media QUALIFICATIONS Qualified candidates will have an interest in and/or knowledge of South Asian literature and cinema, and social justice issues Strong writing and communication skills Completing tasks within assigned deadlines Regular and consistent delivery of assigned tasks Experience with researching, writing, editing Ability to follow direction with minimal supervision Demonstrated strong attention to detail Ability to use MS Office tools including databases for tracking or qualitative and/or quantitative studies Good interpersonal, organization, research skills A professional and positive attitude APPLICATION PROCESS A complete application includes: A resume A statement of interest (300-500 words) that explains why you would like to work on this project A writing sample Please combine the required documents into one single document when submitting your application. *SALARY INFORMATION Anticipated hourly pay rate: $22.00 - $27.00 Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4595": {
      "title": "Student Ambassador, Student Affairs",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Student Ambassador, Student Affairs Department/Faculty Student Services - Student Affairs Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 4 Months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4595 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Communications and Events Coordinator, Student Services. SUMMARY The Student Ambassador is an integral part of Student Services and enhances the KPU student experience with prospective and current students and community members. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Engage with students and campus visitors for wayfinding and referral to services. Provide knowledgeable, timely, and professional customer service. Develop and maintain detailed records of engagements. Assist with content for divisional social media accounts. Assist with event planning, setup, coordination, and logistics. Assist with drafting and reviewing communication and marketing materials. QUALIFICATIONS Good academic standing. Good organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Experience in communications, marketing, and/or a related field is an asset. Proficient in MS Office applications. Familiar with common social media platforms. Reliable, responsible, and professional with a customer-service mindset. Able to work independently and as part of a team. Able to effectively multi-task. Sensitive to the needs of a diverse student population. Available to work across all KPU campuses as needed. Available to work evenings and weekends as needed. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
