    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4844": {
      "title": "Sustainability Data & Communications Support",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Sustainability Data & Communications Support Department/Faculty Office of the VP, Administration Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 7 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4844 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Director of Planning, Development, and Sustainability. SUMMARY The Sustainability Data & Communications Support position will assist the Office of Sustainability in advancing campus sustainability initiatives through data management, digital communications, and on-campus engagement. The successful candidate will assist with maintaining and updating energy and sustainability performance dashboards, support website content updates, and contribute to sustainability reporting and on-campus engagements. This position provides an opportunity for students to gain hands-on experience in sustainability data analysis and sustainability communications and is ideal for a student interested in combining sustainability, data analytics, community engagement, and communications to help advance institutional sustainability goals. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Dashboard and Data Support Assists in updating and maintaining energy, greenhouse gas (GHG), utility, and sustainability performance dashboards. Compiles, organizes, and validates sustainability-related data from various institutional sources. Helps develop new dashboard features and visualizations to improve data accessibility and key party understanding. Website and Communications Support Updates sustainability website content, ensuring information remains accurate, current, and accessible. Gathers, coordinates, and maintains internal and external communications content for KPU's sustainability communication channels. Helps improve the organization and presentation of sustainability information across digital platforms. Sustainability Program Support Supports outreach activities, campaigns, and events promoting sustainability on campus. Provides general administrative support to sustainability projects as needed. QUALIFICATIONS Current KPU student in good academic standing, with a minimum 2.5 GPA Knowledge of sustainability concepts, greenhouse gas accounting, or energy management. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple tasks and work independently. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4827": {
      "title": "System Support Technologist - Help Desk",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description System Support Technologist - Help Desk Department/Faculty IT Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 4 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4827 Internal Closing Date: October 11, 2026 External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 12 - BCGEU Pay Grid - $32.94 to $36.78 per hour Employment Type: Temporary Full Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Support Staff (BC General Employees Union) Days of Work (BCGEU): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday Hours of Work (BCGEU): 9:00am - 5:00pm Hours per Week (BCGEU): 35 We are currently seeking a Systems Support Technologist - Help Desk to join our Information Technology (IT) team. Job Overview To provide computer support services to students and employee users of Kwantlen University College systems. Education and Experience Completion of a Computer Systems Technology diploma or equivalent. Minimum of 2 years' experience working on a computer support service desk using remote control and basic monitoring systems. Minimum of 2 years' experience in identifying, analyzing, diagnosing and resolving complex problems over the phone. Minimum of 2 years' experience in using a technology service management system in an ITIL environment. Proven ability to work in a customer focused computer support service center. 3 years' experience in providing on-site computer desktop and peripheral support including printers, data projectors, laptops, tablets and smart phones. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Proven superior customer service skills. Working knowledge of Exchange, Active Directory and SharePoint. Thorough knowledge of ITIL incident and request management. Thorough knowledge of Microsoft Windows operating systems. Thorough knowledge of standard desktop applications (including word processing, spreadsheet, communications, databases and desktop video conferencing). Proven ability to quickly grasp new concepts and learn new systems. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing. Proven ability to deal effectively with others and to handle unusual or unexpected situations. Proven ability to work under minimal supervision, under own initiative and as an effective team member. Proven ability to independently organize work to achieve predetermined goals and meet deadlines. Possession of a valid driver’s license and access to a vehicle is required. Please click here for a more detailed job description. As per the KPU-BCGEU Collective Agreement, qualified internal applicants within the BCGEU bargaining unit are given first consideration in filling this position. Internal applicants must apply by 11:59pm on the internal closing date in order to be considered as an internal applicant. Internal applications received after the closing date will be considered as an external applicant. Salary Information Salary and wage increments are in accordance with the Collective Agreement . Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4166": {
      "title": "Tutors - Student Assistant - Learning Centre",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Tutors - Student Assistant - Learning Centre Department/Faculty Faculty of Academic & Career Preparation Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 8 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4166 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 38 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to Learning Strategist or Learning Centre Coordinator. SUMMARY Tutors receive three levels of training. Principle duties include tutoring KPU students to help them become more effective learners. Tutors achieve this by asking questions about the student's understanding of the subject area, making suggestions about how to study or a method of approaching a problem, modelling appropriate learning strategies, and by referring the student to learning resources or other services within or outside the university. Peer Tutors are not expected to teach coursework. They are not expected to be substitutes for teachers and they are definitely not allowed to do the student's work or assignments. Peer tutors are current KPU students helping other students to learn. This position is reserved for KPU students only. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES To tutor KPU students in specific subject areas after completing appropriate training To help KPU students to understand main course concepts, how to follow assignment structures, and how to improve their performance in their coursework To provide feedback on students' assignments and to provide students with ways to improve their work To help students to identify and find the assistance they need To assist with transition, orientation and retention programs To assist with the promotion of Learning Centre services and programs QUALIFICATIONS Confident in their knowledge of a specific subject(s) Patient and willing to tailor their explanation of key concepts to a variety of students Friendly and welcoming of all students Punctual, focused, and hard-working Be registered as a KPU student Maintain a minimum GPA of 3.0 and have completed at least 24 credit hours Provide references from two KPU instructors who would support your application Can identify ways in which to learn subject matter effectively Can identify errors in students' understanding of key course concepts Has a clear understanding of the key concepts and skills in the courses and subject areas that they wish to tutor in LOCATION KPU has four learning centers, which are located on the Surrey, Langley, Richmond, and Cloverdale campuses. Tutors can choose which campus they would like to tutor at; however, different tutors are needed at different campuses depending on the subject that they tutor in. Tutors will also be eligible to tutor online. *APPLICATION PROCESS All applications must include: Resume Unofficial Transcript Next Semester Course Schedule Reference Letter *Required documents must be combined into one single document when uploading to your application. *SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4825": {
      "title": "Vice President, Human Resources",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Vice President, Human Resources Department/Faculty Human Resources Home Campus (Location) Surrey Main - Surrey, BC Employment Duration PERMANENT Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4825 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: 18 – Administrative Salary Grid - $166,197 to $254,836 Employment Type: Permanent Full Time Workplace Type: Hybrid Travel Frequency: Frequent travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Administration/Management Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): The Opportunity This is a pivotal moment to join Kwantlen Polytechnic University’s executive leadership team. We are seeking an experienced and visionary Vice President, Human Resources (VP HR) to guide KPU through a period of significant change and renewal. Reporting directly to the President and Vice Chancellor, the VP Human Resources is a trusted advisor and key member of the executive team — shaping the future of KPU’s workforce, advancing organizational strategy, and fostering a strong, inclusive workplace culture. The VP Human Resources provides executive leadership across various positions – Director, HR Systems & Talent Development; the Director, Labour Relations; and the Director, Workforce Advisory & Compensation, as well as the Manager, Campus Security Operations and the Manager, Emergency Planning. This role is both strategic and hands-on, offering the opportunity to influence KPU’s people strategy and support student success, community engagement, and institutional priorities. As VP Human Resources, you will: Serve as a trusted advisor to the President, Board, and senior leadership, guiding people strategies that align with KPU’s mission and long-term priorities. Champion the employee experience, shaping programs and practices that strengthen engagement, learning, well-being, and a sense of belonging across KPU. Lead transformation by modernizing HR practices, introducing innovative approaches, and helping the university evolve through times of change. Provide strategic and operational leadership across all HR functions — including labour relations, recruitment, retention, compensation, organizational development, and employee experience. Working collaboratively with the Office of General Counsel and other institutional partners to identify and manage legal and organizational risk. Provide strategic leadership in complex employment, Human Rights, workplace investigations, regulatory, and labour relations matters, including collective bargaining, grievances, conflict resolution, and building strong, collaborative union relationships. Provide oversight and direction for Risk and Campus Safety & Security, ensuring a safe and supportive environment for students, faculty, and staff. Foster equity, diversity, inclusion, and reconciliation in all aspects of HR strategy and institutional culture. Build strong relationships with faculty, staff, and unions, fostering collaboration, trust, and effective resolution of complex issues in a unionized environment. Oversee, support and mentor a diverse HR leadership team, in order to achieve departmental and institutional goals. Strengthen connections with the communities KPU serves and collaborate with peer post-secondary institutions across BC and Canada to share expertise and advance best practices. Influence institution-wide priorities as part of KPU’s executive leadership team, contributing to a student-focused, community-driven, and inclusive university. What You Bring You are a seasoned HR executive who thrives in complex environments and sees opportunity in times of change. You bring both strategic foresight and operational expertise, with a track record of leading transformation, building strong teams, and fostering inclusive workplaces in a complex unionized environment. You are trusted for your integrity, sound judgment, and ability to inspire confidence at every level of an organization. We’re looking for someone who: Holds a graduate degree in a relevant discipline and has at least 10 years of senior HR leadership experience, ideally in the public sector or post-secondary. Has a proven ability to lead change, modernize practices, and guide teams through transition. Is confident advising Presidents, Boards, and senior leaders on sensitive HR and organizational matters. Builds credibility through integrity, consistency, transparency, and fairness. Demonstrates strong emotional intelligence: listens, engages, and fosters a respectful, inclusive work environment. Is deeply committed to advancing equity, diversity, inclusion, and reconciliation, and to creating a workplace where all employees feel valued and supported. Brings extensive labour relations experience, including collective bargaining, grievances, and arbitration. Has experience developing and empowering high-performing teams, balancing accountability with collaboration and service excellence. Brings resilience, adaptability, and the ability to make sound decisions in a complex, unionized environment. Want to know more? For more detailed information on this position, click here . The Location KPU is a multi-campus institution. The Human Resources offices are located at the Langley campus; however, this position will be based primarily at the Surrey Main campus. Application Process To apply for this opportunity, please submit your cover letter and resume as one document via KPU’s Career Centre.  Resume review will be conducted on October 16, 2026 however, the competition will remain open until filled. For inquiries or recommendations related to this position, please contact: Evita Gandhi Talent Acquisition Specialist Email: evita.gandhi@kpu.ca Salary Information The above compensation range is the span between the minimum and maximum base salary for a position.  Typically, initial salary placement is approximately halfway between the minimum and the maximum.  This represents an employee that possesses full job knowledge, qualifications and experience for the position.  In the normal course, employees will be hired, transferred or promoted between the minimum and approximately halfway of the salary range for a job with consideration given to internal equity. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4828": {
      "title": "Welder Testing Support",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Welder Testing Support Department/Faculty Faculty of Trades & Technology Home Campus (Location) Cloverdale Tech - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 1 year Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4828 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Welder Testing Coordinator. SUMMARY The Student Assistant, Welder Testing Support provides general operational assistance in support of KPU welder testing. The role supports preparation of materials, maintenance of workspaces, and basic logistical tasks that contribute to program delivery, and shop readiness. Work is routine in nature and aligned with foundational skills taught within the program, with tasks completed under supervision and in accordance with established safety procedures. This position is reserved for KPU Students only. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Prepare materials and resources for instructional activities and student assessments. Support setup, organization, and basic cleaning of shop and workspace areas for welder testing. Complete routine entry-level preparation tasks aligned with program coursework (e.g., material or coupon preparation). Provide logistical support during testing, as directed. Monitor basic supply needs and report issues to instructional staff. Follow all safety procedures, including appropriate PPE and tool usage. QUALIFICATIONS Active student within a relevant trades program at the Faculty of Trades and Technology. Familiarity with shop safety practices and appropriate PPE usage through coursework. Ability to perform routine hands-on tasks in a shop environment. Reliable, organized, and able to manage time within scheduled shifts. Demonstrates attention to detail and willingness to support team operations. Able to follow instructions and work both independently and collaboratively. Physically able to perform light material handling and shop support activities. SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4443": {
      "title": "Welding Instructor",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Welding Instructor Department/Faculty Faculty of Trades & Technology Home Campus (Location) Cloverdale Tech - Surrey, BC Employment Duration 1 (one) year on call Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4443 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 1 *Salary Information: Faculty Pay Scale Employment Type: Qualified Faculty List Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Occasional travel between campuses is required. Employee Group: Faculty (Kwantlen Faculty Association) Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): WELDING INSTRUCTOR POSITION TYPE: Qualified Faculty List POSITION START: As soon as possible FACULTY OVERVIEW: Kwantlen Polytechnic University’s Welding program provides students with the necessary training to become professional welders. Students will develop the skill and knowledge to work safely and effectively in today’s demanding industrial environment. POSITION OVERVIEW: The Faculty of Trades and Technology is currently seeking a Non-regular Type 1 Welding Instructor to provide short-term delivery of Apprenticeship Levels 1, 2, and 3, Welding Foundation and/or Levels B and A which may extend from a single day to several weeks. More information concerning the working conditions for a faculty member are outlined in Article 12 of the Kwantlen Faculty Association (KFA) Collective Agreement . QUALIFICATIONS: British Columbia Certificate of Qualification with Interprovincial Red Seal Endorsement. Current BC Pipe Welder Pressure Vessel 7 (PWP7) and BC Pipe Welder Pressure Vessel 10 (PWP10) pressure tickets, or equivalent. A minimum of five years’ experience working in the industry as a journeyperson. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS: Candidates will be required to undergo a Criminal Record Check. *SALARY INFORMATION: Placement on the salary scale will be dependent on level of education and relevant teaching experience. Advancement up the pay scale is based on FTE and employment status. This competition is for successful candidates to be added to our Qualified Faculty List. When work in this area becomes available, our faculty will draw on our Qualified Faculty List to assign work, please indicate on your application your preferred workload percentage. Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=JT63GS&cws=37&rid=4787": {
      "title": "Wilson School of Design Student Assistant (Generalist with Specializations)",
      "description": "Career Centre New Search Log-in Page Position Description Wilson School of Design Student Assistant (Generalist with Specializations) Department/Faculty Wilson School of Design Home Campus (Location) Richmond, BC Employment Duration 3.5 months Apply Now Kwantlen Polytechnic University (KPU) is Canada’s only polytechnic university, proudly serving the South Fraser region for more than 40 years. With campuses in Surrey, Richmond, Langley, and Cloverdale, KPU is deeply connected to the communities it serves and to the diverse cultures, backgrounds, and lived experiences of its students. Through academic excellence, applied learning, innovation, and strong industry and community partnerships, KPU prepares students for meaningful futures. As an open-access university, KPU is powered by the people who live and work here. We believe every employee plays a meaningful role in supporting student learning and success. We are honoured to carry the name of the Kwantlen First Nation and are committed to equity, inclusion, reconciliation, and respectful relationships. As one of BC’s Top Employers, KPU is dedicated to fostering a supportive, inclusive, and engaged workplace where employees feel valued, connected to purpose, and empowered to make an impact. We invite you to explore your next career opportunity at KPU and discover how your work can contribute to a university where thought truly meets action. Competition ID: 4787 Internal Closing Date: Open Until Filled External Closing Date: Open Until Filled # of Openings: 2 *Salary Information: Student Assistant Pay Scale Employment Type: Temporary Part Time Workplace Type: On-Site Travel Frequency: Employee Group: Student Assistant Days of Work (BCGEU): Hours of Work (BCGEU): Hours per Week (BCGEU): ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE This role reports to the Wilson School of Design Dean’s Office. SUMMARY The Student Assistant supports a range of activities within the Wilson School of Design (WSD), contributing to student success, operations, and community engagement. This role is designed as a flexible, multi-functional position, where students may work across different areas or be assigned a primary specialization based on skills, experience, and operational needs. Student Assistants play a key role in fostering a welcoming, inclusive, and dynamic environment by supporting student learning, events, communications, labs, and peer engagement initiatives. This position is reserved for KPU students only. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES (for all Student Assistants) Represent WSD as a positive, professional ambassador at events and within the community Provide excellent customer service and respectful, timely support to students, faculty, staff, and visitors Assist with general operational tasks including setup, coordination, and logistics Support promotion and communication of WSD activities and resources Maintain organized, safe, and welcoming environments across spaces and activities Work both independently and collaboratively while managing time effectively Attend training sessions, team meetings, and professional development opportunities as required Perform additional related duties as assigned AREAS OF SPECIALIZATION Students hired for this position will be assigned to the Peer Mentorship and Student Engagement stream in support of the Wilson Collective initiative. You may be asked to support one of the other streams if needed. 1. Peer Mentorship & Student Engagement Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Provide peer support, guidance, and mentorship to students Share information about academic resources, student services, and wellness supports Foster a sense of belonging and community among WSD students Participate in outreach, community-building initiatives, and student engagement 2. Events & Communications Support Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Assist with planning, coordination, and execution of events (e.g., recruitment, community, student life) Support event logistics including setup, takedown, and on-site coordination Engage with current and prospective students and external community members Contribute to the promotion and documentation of events (photography/video/social media) for web platforms 3. Labs & Technical/Studio Support Under the supervision and direction of the Dean's Office designate: Provide general support for lab, workshop, and studio activities Assist with non-specialized preparation and set-up tasks for classes, projects, and events Help communicate established procedures and direct students to appropriate resources Assist with tours, exhibitions, displays, installations, and special events Observe and report equipment, facility, or safety concerns to supervisory staff Support equipment use and lab operations that are supportive in nature QUALIFICATIONS Currently enrolled student at the Wilson School of Design Strong oral and written communication and interpersonal skills Organized, reliable, self-motivated, and detail-oriented Ability to work independently and collaboratively Comfortable engaging with diverse audiences and communities Interest in student life, community engagement, or design environments ASSETS (vary by specialization): Experience with events, communications, or social media Experience in peer mentoring or leadership roles Familiarity with lab equipment, tools, or creative production processes Working knowledge of Microsoft Office, Adobe Creative Cloud, and WordPress *SALARY INFORMATION Student Assistants are paid as per the following: Less than one year of post-secondary (less than 30 credits) – BC Minimum Wage One year of post-secondary (30-60 credits) – BC Minimum Wage plus 8% With a post-secondary diploma or degree – BC Minimum Wage plus 21% Total Rewards As a part of our total rewards offerings, KPU also offers extended health and dental benefits, healthcare spending account, generous vacation package, defined pension plan, parenthood top-up, sick leave, long-term disability, life insurance, professional development days, tuition waiver, inhouse training & development, inter-campus transportation, and more! Note: Eligibility requirements apply, benefits may vary depending on the employee group the position belongs to and whether the position offered is temporary or part-time. Visit https://www.kpu.ca/hr for more information on KPU’s workplace, culture and total rewards. Note to Applicants Kwantlen Polytechnic University welcomes and encourages applications from equity deserving groups and diverse experiences including, but not limited to, Indigenous people, racialized people, people with disabilities, and members of the 2S/LGBTQIA+ community. If there are any barriers that you are experiencing or an accommodation that we can provide to support you through the application process, please reach out to us at talentacquisition@kpu.ca . Kwantlen Polytechnic University is committed to protecting the safety and welfare of employees, students, and the general public, and upholding the reputation and integrity of the University. For this reason, final applicants will be asked to undergo a background check. We thank all applicants for their interest in employment with KPU. Only candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada will be considered; only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now"
